# Cursor AI Rules for apps/api

> **Extends:** [Root .cursorrules](../../.cursorrules)

## App Context

This is the **Fastify API server** for Xala/Digilist Platform.

**Critical:** All mutations require audit logging. All queries must be tenant-scoped.

## API-Specific Rules

### 1. RFC 7807 Error Format (REQUIRED)
```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT - RFC 7807 compliant
return reply.status(404).send({
  type: '/errors/not-found',
  title: 'Resource Not Found',
  status: 404,
  detail: `Listing with ID ${id} not found`,
});

// ❌ WRONG - Non-compliant error
return reply.status(404).send({ error: 'Not found' });
```

### 2. Audit Logging (REQUIRED)
```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT - Audit all mutations
import { auditLog } from '../utils/audit';

async function updateResource(request, reply) {
  const resource = await db.update(resources)
    .set(updates)
    .where(eq(resources.id, id));

  await auditLog({
    action: 'resource:update',
    resourceType: 'resource',
    resourceId: id,
    userId: request.user.id,
    tenantId: request.tenant.id,
    changes: updates,
  });

  return resource;
}
```

### 3. Tenant Isolation (REQUIRED)
```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT - Tenant-scoped query
const listings = await db.select()
  .from(listings)
  .where(
    and(
      eq(listings.tenantId, request.tenant.id),
      eq(listings.userId, request.user.id)
    )
  );

// ❌ WRONG - No tenant isolation
const listings = await db.select().from(listings);
```

### 4. Input Validation (REQUIRED)
```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT - Zod validation
import { z } from 'zod';

const createSchema = z.object({
  title: z.string().min(3).max(200),
  price: z.number().positive(),
});

const data = createSchema.parse(request.body);
```

### 5. Rate Limiting
```typescript
// ✅ REQUIRED for user-facing endpoints
fastify.route({
  method: 'POST',
  url: '/api/bookings',
  config: {
    rateLimit: {
      max: 10,
      timeWindow: '1 minute',
    },
  },
  handler: createBooking,
});
```

## File Organization

```
src/
├── modules/              # Feature modules
│   ├── auth/
│   ├── listings/
│   ├── bookings/
│   └── users/
├── db/
│   ├── schema/           # Drizzle schemas
│   └── migrations/       # Database migrations
├── middleware/           # Fastify middleware
├── websocket/            # WebSocket server
└── main.ts               # Entry point
```

## Database (Drizzle ORM)

```typescript
// Define schema
export const listings = pgTable('listings', {
  id: uuid('id').primaryKey().defaultRandom(),
  tenantId: uuid('tenant_id').notNull(),
  title: varchar('title', { length: 200 }).notNull(),
});

// Query with Drizzle
const listings = await db.select()
  .from(listings)
  .where(eq(listings.tenantId, tenantId));
```

## WebSocket Events

```typescript
import { websocketServer } from '../websocket';

// Broadcast event
websocketServer.broadcast({
  event: 'booking:created',
  tenantId: booking.tenantId,
  data: booking,
});
```

## Testing

- Unit tests: Co-located `*.test.ts`
- E2E tests: `tests/e2e/`

## Common Mistakes to Avoid

❌ Missing audit logging for mutations
❌ Missing tenant isolation in queries
❌ Non-RFC 7807 error responses
❌ Missing input validation
❌ Missing rate limiting
❌ Hardcoded tenant IDs or user IDs
❌ No WebSocket events for real-time updates

## Required Middleware

- `authMiddleware` - JWT validation
- `tenantMiddleware` - Tenant isolation
- `auditMiddleware` - Audit logging
- `errorMiddleware` - RFC 7807 errors
- `rateLimitMiddleware` - Rate limiting

## Database Commands

```bash
pnpm db:generate    # Generate migrations
pnpm db:migrate     # Run migrations
pnpm db:seed        # Seed data
pnpm db:studio      # Open GUI
```

